      "id": "emergent_industrial_retooling_initiative",
      "description": "In response to the Taiwan blockade, major European industrial firms and national governments begin an emergency initiative to retool existing semiconductor fabrication plants for AI-adjacent workloads using hybrid architectures and relaxed precision requirements. This effort focuses on maximizing utility from available non-frontier chips, aiming to reduce dependency on cutting-edge imports. The initiative gains traction due to shared urgency but faces coordination hurdles across member states.",
